# Line-ending policy (single source of truth, overrides per-machine core.autocrlf)
#
# Background: Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which converts LF<->CRLF
# on checkout/commit. This caused phantom "modified" status on Cargo.toml
# because Cargo / rust-analyzer rewrite the file as LF, fighting autocrlf's
# expectation of CRLF in the working tree.
#
# Fix: force LF for all text files in BOTH the repo blob and the working tree.
# This matches what Rust, Node, and the Vercel/Tauri toolchains emit, so tools
# and git never disagree. Binary files (png/ico/etc.) are auto-detected and
# left untouched.
#
# After changing this file, run:
#   git add --renormalize .
#   git checkout-index --force --all
* text=auto eol=lf
